{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792332170,"nonce":"/BU7mq+n+rxwFWQ7WQSWdfsHPCo=","title":"TreeView: a `guides=\"hover\"` value, so indent guides show on hover without an app's selector override","message":"**What is wanted**\nRayDE hides and shows the indent guides with a CSS override on `.ui-tree-group` under `#rayde-tree:hover`, which works. A `guides=\"hover\"` value on TreeView would give every app that without the override.\n\n**Related, to check**\nA transition on border-color in that rule did not show in an offscreen Snapshot capture: the guides stayed transparent. Whether Snapshot advances transition time is not known; check it, since a captured state that differs from the live one misleads.\n\n**Reported by** chimpmonk-af, RayDE session.","files":null}]}